  "type": "npc",
  "img": "icons/svg/mystery-man.svg",
  "system": {
    "biography": "<p>The new men are nothing more than gangsters and ruffians. The old bosses prefer influence-peddling and embarrassment tactics over the crude intimidation and violence favored by the new blood. Still philosophizing and courteous, if always seeking to spread a veneer of culture and gentility over his rough edges.</p>\n<p><strong>Cyberware:</strong> Datajack, with 60 Mp of Memory, Wired Reflexes (1)</p>\n<p><strong>Augmented:</strong> reaction 7 — The book lists Wired Reflexes (1) but prints Reaction 5 with no augmented figure in parentheses — every other wired contact on these pages prints one. 5 is the unaugmented base ((Quickness 4 + Intelligence 6) / 2), so the parenthetical was omitted. The cyberware is listed, so its effect is applied: +2 Reaction and +1D6 Initiative, the same as the Company Man.</p>\n<p><strong>Professional Rating:</strong> 3-4 (the sheet stores 3; the book prints a range)</p>\n<p><em>Shadowrun, Second Edition, p.213.</em></p>",
